   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "אֲבָל פּוֹתֵחַ הוּא לִרְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים פֶּתַח כְּנֶגֶד פֶּתַח. דְּאָמַר לֵיהּ: סוֹף סוֹף, הָא בָּעֵית אִצְטְנוֹעֵי מִבְּנֵי רְשׁוּת הָרַבִּים.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «But» one «may open an entrance opposite» another «entrance» or a window opposite another window «toward the public domain.» Why is this so? «Because» he can «say to» the one who wishes to protest: «Ultimately, you must conceal yourself from» the «people of the public domain.» Since you cannot stop them from passing by and therefore cannot engage in behavior that requires privacy with your entrance open, it is of no consequence to you if I open an entrance as well."
  }
